00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:02,420
B1.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:07,750
Simon is learning about the weather in different places around the world.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:18,600
Here is a recording about the weather in December in four different cities – Moscow, Shanghai, Cairo and Sydney.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,430
Listen with Simon and complete the table below.

5
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:32,620
In December, the average temperature in Moscow, Russia, is usually below zero degrees.

6
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:38,720
There is a lot of snow and the weather is cold, wet and windy.

7
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:47,320
The city is quite dark at the start of winter, with only about six or seven hours of daylight every day.

8
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:55,540
In Shanghai, China, the average temperature in December is a few degrees above zero.

9
00:00:55,540 --> 00:01:01,100
Because it is next to the sea, Shanghai does not get very cold.

10
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:04,750
Winter in Shanghai can be quite wet.

11
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:08,140
It often rains, but seldom snows.

12
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:18,770
In Cairo, Egypt, December is a winter month, but it is not cold, with an average temperature above ten degrees Celsius.

13
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:23,530
The weather is often nice, but is usually cloudy.

14
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:27,760
December is a summer month in Sydney, Australia.

15
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:36,240
It usually has an average temperature above twenty degrees Celsius, but it is sometimes much hotter.

16
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,450
The weather is great.

17
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:45,130
On average, there are about nine hours of sunshine every day, and not much rain.
